DECISION CliDoesTheMechanicalWorkAgentsOnlyJudge
	TITLE "every mechanical step of a wave is a CLI command; a model is called only to judge"
	STATUS active
	DESC "branches, worktrees, ordering, launching, polling, merging, rebasing, statistics, report"
		+ "skeletons and signal normalisation are deterministic Python; an agent receives a"
		+ "pre-computed context from one command and returns a verdict or a text through another"
	REJECTED "a coordinator agent that orchestrates the wave: it rediscovers state at every step"
		+ "and spends judgment on bookkeeping"
	REJECTED "letting each run read git, gh and files itself: measured, the first edit of a task"
		+ "run came after 23 steps and 134 000 tokens in median"
	RATIONALE "the user's first principle for the plan; the measured cost of discovery is the"
		+ "largest saving available"
	SOURCE "the Artifact Brigade Blueprint, plan section 1 and 5"

DECISION TheToolIsNamedBrigade
	TITLE "the CLI, the repository and the config directory are named brigade"
	STATUS active
	DESC "the kitchen brigade is the team of roles under the chef, who is the user; the"
		+ "verification gate is nicknamed the pass"
	REJECTED "fab: collides with the Fabric CLI"
	REJECTED "chef, kitchen: collide with the Chef ecosystem's CLIs"
	REJECTED "expo, pass: collide with the Expo CLI and the pass password store"
	RATIONALE "free on PATH and in Debian packages on 2026-10-04; the metaphor is the one the user"
		+ "adopted from the talk"
	SOURCE "the Artifact Brigade Blueprint, plan section 3"

DECISION PythonStandardLibraryOnly
	TITLE "brigade is Python 3.13 standard library plus POSIX sh for systemd units, with no"
		+ "third-party dependency"
	STATUS active
	REJECTED "a Bun or TypeScript CLI: ties a machine-wide tool to a JavaScript toolchain the"
		+ "instructions corpus does not have"
	REJECTED "a TUI framework: a new dependency for views the web dashboard renders"
	REJECTED "Rust: a single binary to distribute and the compiler as verifier, but no cargo or"
		+ "rustc on the machine, third-party crates in practice, slower agent iteration and none of"
		+ "the existing tooling in Rust; the command-line contract keeps the migration open"
	RATIONALE "the hooks, the unattended runner and the user's local context page are already"
		+ "Python and sh; nothing new has to be installed"
	SOURCE "the Artifact Brigade Blueprint, plan section 13 and 14"

DECISION ADeterministicTickReplacesTheCoordinatorAgent
	TITLE "the coordinator is brigade tick, a deterministic pass run by a user systemd timer every"
		+ "five minutes"
	STATUS active
	DESC "it reconciles waves with git and GitHub, advances task states, launches runs within the"
		+ "slot cap, merges verified pull requests and records events"
	REJECTED "a long-lived coordinator session: costs tokens for waiting and loses state at"
		+ "compaction"
	REJECTED "cloud routines: the private satellite and the worktrees are on the machine only"
	RATIONALE "every transition is a condition evaluated from facts; the laptop being off loses"
		+ "nothing with Persistent=true"
	SOURCE "the Artifact Brigade Blueprint, plan section 5 and 15"

DECISION HybridStorageCorpusAndLedger
	TITLE "durable facts live in awawa corpora, high-volume events in an append-only JSONL ledger"
	STATUS active
	DESC "the brigade corpus holds PROJECT, POLICY, ROUTINE, REQUEST, PATTERN and CONSTRAINT; each"
		+ "project corpus keeps its WAVE and TASK entities; the ledger holds runs, states, pauses"
		+ "and merges"
	REJECTED "everything in awawa: one entity per run means thousands of entities and git noise"
	REJECTED "SQLite for everything: a second grammar without schema lint"
	RATIONALE "the user's answer to the storage question; one home per fact, views rendered never"
		+ "hand-maintained"
	SOURCE "the Artifact Brigade Blueprint, plan section 11 and 12"

DECISION AVerifierRunOnEveryPullRequestAndOneHumanGate
	TITLE "every pull request passes a deterministic preflight then one prudence run before merging"
		+ "into integration; the user merges integration into main"
	STATUS active
	REJECTED "the user reviewing every diff: the rung the user asked to leave"
	REJECTED "sampling that blocks: sampling stays a suggestion in the report"
	RATIONALE "the user's answers on autonomy and review; delivered work is never verified by the"
		+ "run that produced it"
	SOURCE "the Artifact Brigade Blueprint, plan section 7"

DECISION QuotaPausesTheWaveAndResumesTheSameSession
	TITLE "a rate-limit result pauses the wave; the resume is the adapter's resume of the suspended"
		+ "session at the time the message names"
	STATUS active
	REJECTED "a dollar cap: the subscription is the cap"
	REJECTED "probing the quota with extra calls: the resume itself is the probe"
	RATIONALE "the user's answer on budget: waves of 10 to 20 pull requests, the quota blocks"
		+ "before any overspend"
	SOURCE "the Artifact Brigade Blueprint, plan section 15"

DECISION TheDashboardIsBuiltThePluginAndAwawaWebAreKept
	TITLE "a loopback web dashboard is built; the IntelliJ plugin stays for in-IDE work; awawa-web"
		+ "stays the editor of the brigade corpus"
	STATUS active
	DESC "the dashboard exposes a local JSON API the plugin may consume later for a branch selector"
	REJECTED "extending the plugin into the factory's UI: it would have to grow a server and a"
		+ "ledger reader of its own"
	REJECTED "a second corpus editor in the dashboard: awawa-web already edits block by block with"
		+ "fmt and lint"
	RATIONALE "the plugin's handbook names user-defined views as its extension point; the branch"
		+ "selector is a server-side fact (git archive per SHA)"
	SOURCE "the Artifact Brigade Blueprint, plan section 13"

DECISION AwawaIsWrappedAsItIs
	TITLE "the plan wraps the awawa binary as it is; desired changes go to a list of requests to"
		+ "its author, never on the critical path"
	STATUS active
	REJECTED "forking awawa or waiting for a feature: the user is a consumer and the author may"
		+ "lack time"
	RATIONALE "every awawa gap has a workaround the POC uses: block edits with fmt and lint,"
		+ "per-entity spawns cached per SHA"
	SOURCE "the Artifact Brigade Blueprint, plan section 17"

DECISION MinedConstraintsAreDeliveredAsWaves
	TITLE "constraints mined from transcripts become waves like any other work, auto-merged into"
		+ "integration and listed in the report with their reason"
	STATUS active
	DESC "the scrubber runs before anything leaves the state directory: Steam id pattern, player"
		+ "names computed at run time from the private saves and never stored, e-mail addresses,"
		+ "private paths"
	REJECTED "proposals only in the dashboard: the user asked for the same autonomy as a wave"
	REJECTED "a stored list of real names for the scrubber: no correspondence between a real name"
		+ "and a pseudonym is kept anywhere"
	RATIONALE "the user's answer on mining; the anonymisation rule of the example project"
	SOURCE "the Artifact Brigade Blueprint, plan section 10"

DECISION TheCorpusIsTheHomeOfTaskStatusTheBoardItsView
	TITLE "the corpus is the single home of task status; the task board of the Artifact is a view"
		+ "of it"
	STATUS active
	DESC "a task's STATUS is edited in docs/tasks.awawa and nowhere else"
	DESC "the board of the Blueprint shows the status the corpus holds, written by a deterministic"
		+ "command"
	DESC "a status changed on the board binds nothing"
	REJECTED "the board as the home of status until the brigade delivers its own waves, the"
		+ "planning run's choice: the corpus held every task draft while the board showed them"
		+ "todo, two homes already disagreeing"
	REJECTED "two homes kept in sync by hand: a hand-maintained view is wrong by the next commit"
	RATIONALE "the plan's own principle, one home per fact, views rendered never hand-maintained;"
		+ "ruled by the user on 2026-10-05"
	SOURCE "pull request #1 of the brigade repository"

DECISION BrigadeNamesNoAgentCliEachCliIsAnAdapter
	TITLE "the core of brigade names no agent CLI; each CLI is an adapter behind one interface, and"
		+ "Claude Code is the first adapter"
	STATUS active
	DESC "the interface: launch a run as a role with a brief, capabilities and a budget, detached;"
		+ "return a normalised result (steps, duration, usage, session id, error kind, the reset"
		+ "time of a rate limit); resume a session; read session transcripts for the miner"
	DESC "a run is launched detached under systemd-run with the adapter's headless mode"
	DESC "a flag, a hook, a session file or a command of one CLI appears only in its adapter"
	REJECTED "brigade as the one place where the first CLI's flags, hooks and session files are"
		+ "known, the plan's sixth principle of 2026-10-04: a second CLI would rewrite every"
		+ "command"
	REJECTED "the attachable background sessions of one CLI (claude --bg) as the way to run long"
		+ "runs: a feature of one adapter, not of the core; the adapter's resume is the way back in"
	RATIONALE "the user ruled on 2026-10-05 that the plan be reviewed to be agnostic and avoid what"
		+ "is specific to one agent CLI; the instructions corpus holds the same stance for itself"
		+ "in @RULE.instructions_are_agent_agnostic"
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-05, pull request #2 of the brigade repository"

DECISION TheMergeMethodIsTheInstructionsCorpusRuleNotAProjectField
	TITLE "the merge of a task pull request into the integration branch follows the merge rule of"
		+ "the instructions corpus; the brigade corpus declares no merge field"
	STATUS active
	DESC "the rule is @RULE.squash_merge_rebase_update of the instructions corpus; the tick merges"
		+ "with the method it names, a constant of the tick; the rule is cited, never restated"
	REJECTED "PROJECT.MERGE squash|rebase|merge per project, the plan's field of 2026-10-04: a"
		+ "general rule copied into every project's record, two homes for one fact"
	RATIONALE "the user ruled the merge method general on 2026-10-05; a general rule lives in the"
		+ "instructions corpus and in no project's records"
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-05, pull request #2 of the brigade repository"
	SOURCE "@RULE.squash_merge_rebase_update, written by pull request #73 of the instructions"
		+ "repository"

DECISION TheIntegrationPullRequestOpensAsLateAsPossible
	TITLE "the integration pull request is opened as late as possible, with the report; earlier"
		+ "when a need requires it"
	STATUS active
	DESC "the tick opens it when the report is committed on the integration branch"
	REJECTED "opening it at the wave's start for visible progress, its body rewritten by each"
		+ "report, the plan's proposal of 2026-10-04: the user prefers it opened as late as"
		+ "possible"
	RATIONALE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-05 on the open decision of plan section 19"
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-05, pull request #2 of the brigade repository"

DECISION PlanReviewAsksForTheFirstWavesOfANewProject
	TITLE "PLAN_REVIEW is ask for the first waves of a newly registered project, then auto"
	STATUS active
	DESC "the schema default is ask: a POLICY that names no PLAN_REVIEW asks"
	DESC "the switch to auto is an edit of the POLICY"
	REJECTED "auto as the schema default, the plan's proposal of 2026-10-04: the first plans of a"
		+ "project are the ones the user has not yet seen"
	RATIONALE "the user's answer of 2026-10-05 to the open decision of plan section 19"
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-05, pull request #2 of the brigade repository"

DECISION BrigadeDeliversItsOwnWavesFromM2
	TITLE "milestones M0 and M1 are delivered by the existing machinery, one pull request per task;"
		+ "from M2 brigade delivers its own waves"
	STATUS active
	DESC "the existing machinery is the roles of the instructions corpus, launched by hand"
	REJECTED "the existing machinery for every milestone: brigade would never be its own first user"
	REJECTED "dogfooding from the first milestone: the wave engine exists only once M1 is delivered"
	RATIONALE "the user confirmed on 2026-10-05 the plan's proposal of dogfooding from M2"
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-05, pull request #2 of the brigade repository"

DECISION BrigadeIsShareableFromTheStart
	TITLE "brigade is shareable from the start: no path and no account in the code, the machine"
		+ "account optional, Linux with user systemd, default roles for a user without an"
		+ "instructions corpus; the installation on another machine is a milestone after the POC"
	STATUS active
	DESC "every path and every account comes from the config corpus: SETTINGS and PROJECT"
	DESC "the machine account is optional: without one, gh runs as the user's account"
	DESC "systemd is the only scheduler; there is no launchd adapter"
	DESC "brigade init asks whether to import the roles the user defines or to use brigade's"
		+ "default roles"
	DESC "brigade ships a minimal set of default roles and the rules they need, usable without the"
		+ "user's instructions corpus"
	DESC "awawa stays a prerequisite that doctor checks"
	DESC "the installation on another Linux machine, documented, is milestone M7, after M0 to M6"
	REJECTED "sharing as a concern after the POC: paths and accounts written into the code would"
		+ "have to be dug out of every command"
	REJECTED "a launchd adapter for macOS: the other user works on Linux"
	REJECTED "the machine account required: one more account to create before the first wave"
	RATIONALE "the user intends to share the tool with a friend, who works on Linux, once it is"
		+ "finished; on 2026-10-05 the user chose the objective from now on, with the installation"
		+ "as a milestone after the POC"
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-05, pull request #2 of the brigade repository"

DECISION TheCommandLineIsTheContract
	TITLE "brigade's contract is its command-line interface: the shapes of its --json outputs and"
		+ "of its state files are CONTRACT entities of this corpus, never a Python-specific format"
	STATUS active
	DESC "every command is tested as a black box, a subprocess in and JSON out, besides its unit"
		+ "tests"
	DESC "adapters and hooks talk to brigade by subprocess and JSON, never by Python import"
	DESC "no pickle, no serialised object: a state file is JSON, JSON lines or text"
	REJECTED "a Python API as the contract: a migration to another language would rewrite every"
		+ "caller"
	RATIONALE "the contract keeps a later migration, to Rust or another language, open; the choice"
		+ "of Python stands"
	SOURCE "the user's ruling of 2026-10-05 on sharing, pull request #2 of the brigade repository"
